}

@Override @Transactional(readOnly = true)
public Collection<Owner> findAllOwners() throws DataAccessException {
    return ownerRepository.findAll();
}
```
If you add a repository lookup-by-telephone, you would surface it here as a new `ClinicService` method delegating to the repository.

### 3. Owner entity / telephone field
File: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain4/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`
```java
@Column(name = "telephone")
@NotEmpty
@Digits(fraction = 0, integer = 10)
@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{10}$", message = "Phone number must be exactly 10 digits")
private String telephone;
```
Getter `getTelephone()` at lines 71-73. `Owner extends Person` (lastName/firstName live on `Person`).

### 4. Owner repository (Spring Data JPA) and existing query methods
Base interface: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain4/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`
Methods: `findByLastName(String)`, `findByLastName(String, Pageable)`, `findById(int)`, `save(Owner)`, `findAll()`, `findAll(Pageable)`, `delete(Owner)`. No telephone query exists yet.

Spring Data impl: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain4/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java` (active under `@Profile("spring-data-jpa")`). Existing `@Query` methods for lastName/findAll/findById. This is where you would add e.g. a `@Query("SELECT owner FROM Owner owner WHERE owner.telephone = :telephone")` finder.

Other repo implementations that also implement `OwnerRepository` (would need the same new method if you add it to the base interface): `.../repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java` and `.../repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`. If you add the telephone check purely in the controller using existing methods, you can avoid touching these.

### 5. Duplicate / validation error handling and 409 patterns
- Existing 409 pattern: the only place returning `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` / `isDuplicateOwner` shown above (controller returns `new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT)` directly — no exception thrown).
- Global handler: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain4/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java` (`@ControllerAdvice`). Handles:
  - `AccessDeniedException` → rethrown (403 via Spring Security)
  - generic `Exception` → 500
  - `DataIntegrityViolationException` → 404 (returns `ProblemDetail`)
  - `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → 400 (bean-validation field errors, `schemaValidationErrors`)
  - There is NO exception-based 409 handler; the conflict is currently done inline in the controller. If you prefer an exception-driven approach you would add a new `@ExceptionHandler` here, otherwise follow the existing inline `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` pattern.

### 6. Existing tests for owner creation
Controller tests: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain4/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`
Relevant cases:
- `createOwnerSuccess` (line 104) → 201 Created
- `createOwnerDuplicateLastNameAndTelephoneReturnsConflict` (line 117) → expects 409 (currently keyed on same lastName + same telephone)
- `createOwnerSameLastNameDifferentTelephoneSucceeds` (line 130) → expects 201. NOTE: this test would need revisiting — if you switch to telephone-only uniqueness it still uses a different telephone so it stays 201, but any test that relies on "same telephone + different lastName succeeds" would now need to expect 409. There is a `newOwner(...)` helper used to seed owners (telephone `6085551023`).

Service tests: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain4/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/clinicService/AbstractClinicServiceTests.java`
- `shouldInsertOwner` (line 82) uses `saveOwner` + `findOwnerByLastName`
- `shouldUpdateOwner` (line 101), `shouldFindOwnersByLastName` (line 63), `shouldFindAllOwners` (line 330), `shouldDeleteOwner` (line 360)

Also relevant: acceptance tests under `.../src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/` (Cp01/Cp02/Cp03Tests, AcceptanceBase) reference Owner and may exercise creation end-to-end.

### Summary for your implementation
The 409-on-duplicate scaffolding already exists in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` via `isDuplicateOwner`. To reject an owner whose telephone is already used by ANY other owner, the minimal change is to modify `isDuplicateOwner` to match on telephone only and to source candidate owners from all owners (or add a `findByTelephone` query to `OwnerRepository` + `SpringDataOwnerRepository` + `ClinicService`/`ClinicServiceImpl`, plus the JPA/JDBC impls if you extend the base interface). Then update/add tests in `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests` (especially `createOwnerSameLastNameDifferentTelephoneSucceeds` and the duplicate test naming).

